      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>Imported for the first time from Paraguay. Most probably it represents a population of Macrobrachium brasiliense. The maximum length of the animals is around 5 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>Compared with the Peruvian specimens, those from Paraguay have more slender arms, otherwise they look identical. Possibly the species will now become more widespread in aquaria than before.</p><p>Lexicon: Macrobrachium: ancient Greek, means \"with big arm\". brasiliense: means \"coming from Brazil\".</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>Paraguay. The species was also imported occasionally from Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>Animals from the Paraguay system are not as demanding regarding water chemistry as those from the Amazon/Orinoco system and can be kept very well at a pH higher than 7.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_paraguay_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species can be easily bred in freshwater.</p>"
    }
